        "content": "{\n  \"status\": \"partial\",\n  \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n  \"useful_material\": \"该综述明确指出目前缺乏针对肌苷在结直肠癌（CRC）发展过程中空间分布的标准化临床测量研究，大部分数据来源于批量代谢组学分析（bulk metabolomic analysis），且无人研究纵向追踪肌苷水平。文中提到仅有一项混合实体瘤的 II 期临床试验使用了口服肌苷补充（0.2 g，每日三次），但未报告针对 CRC 亚组的内源性浓度测量协议或参考范围。此外，文章强调了肌苷在肠腔与组织间的空间重编程及在炎症 - 肿瘤轴上的时序功能变化，解释了为何单一浓度测量可能不足以反映其生理状态，间接支持了建立标准化测量方法的必要性及当前处于'partial'或缺失状态的判断。\",\n  \"auxiliary_material\": \"文章详细描述了肌苷的化学性质（极性、水溶性、pH 稳定性）、来源（宿主 ADA 酶解、特定菌群如 Bifidobacterium pseudolongum 产生）及信号通路（A2A 受体、cAMP/PKA）。提供了肌苷在肿瘤微环境中的双重作用机制：既可通过 TGF-β1/LACC1 轴促进癌细胞 EMT 和作为碳源支持肿瘤生存，也可通过激活 T 细胞和 M1 巨噬细胞增强免疫检查点抑制剂疗效。这些机制细节有助于理解为何需要区分不同微环境 compartment（肠腔 vs 组织）的浓度测量。\",\n  \"remaining_gap\": \"仍未找到人体肿瘤微环境或血清中肌苷绝对生理浓度的标准化测量协议、具体参考范围或共识声明。现有临床数据仅限于外源性补充试验，缺乏内源性基线浓度的标准化分层数据（如 CheckMate 025 队列式的代谢物分层）。短链脂肪酸（SCFA）的测量方法在本材料中未涉及。\",\n  \"outline_action\": \"在综述中引用该材料以证实肌苷测量方法的当前缺失状态和复杂性（空间/时序重编程），作为论证需要建立标准化测量协议的依据。需继续检索专门的方法学论文、代谢组学共识声明或包含详细生物标志物检测方案的临床试验方案（如 CheckMate 系列或其他 ICI 试验的附属代谢组学研究），以寻找具体的标准化流程或参考范围。\"\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "The user wants me to analyze a provided paper text against a specific gap question and success criteria.\n\n**Gap Question:** \"人体肿瘤微环境或血清中关键代谢物（肌苷、短链脂肪酸）的绝对生理浓度标准化测量方法是否已建立？\" (Have standardized measurement methods for absolute physiological concentrations of key metabolites (inosine, short-chain fatty acids) in human tumor microenvironment or serum been established?)\n\n**Success Criteria:**\n1. Find specific standardized measurement protocols, reference ranges, or consensus statements.\n2. Or confirm it remains in a 'partial' state (e.g., only stratified data like CheckMate 025 cohort).\n\n**Status Options:** fulfilled, partial, unmet, unjudgeable.\n**Material Usefulness Options:** direct, supporting, none.\n\n**Task:**\n1. Describe what the supplied paper studied and found.\n2. Explain how that material helps with the requested gap.\n3. Keep primary gap judgment separate from material usefulness.\n4. Do not call the gap fulfilled if a success criterion remains open.\n5. Return one JSON object.\n\n**Analysis of the Paper:**\n- **Type:** Review article (states \"This review summarizes...\", \"Methodology... comprehensive literature search...\").\n- **Topic:** Inosine's role in gut homeostasis and colorectal cancer (CRC), specifically its spatial/temporal reprogramming and interaction with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI).\n- **Findings regarding measurement:**\n    - Section 4.1: \"Unfortunately, studies reporting the effects of the spatial redistribution of inosine across different intestinal compartments along CRC onset are currently missing since most of the clinical and preclinical data were generated from a bulk metabolomic analysis [33,35].\"\n    - Section 4.2: \"Currently, no human studies have longitudinally tracked inosine levels or purine metabolic flux from colitis through dysplasia to established CRC.\"\n    - Section 4.4: Mentions one phase-2 clinical trial where inosine was supplemented (0.2 g orally), but does not de